---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Alloy Procurement Planner"
  description="Avery Moon designed an 18-month material planning system connecting customer demand, alloy inventory, scheduled receipts, purchasing constraints, and supplier forecasting."
>
<section class="case-hero case-alloy">
  <div class="container">
    <a class="case-back" href={`${base}/built-systems/`}>← Built Systems</a>
    <div class="case-kicker">01 / Material Planning</div>
    <h1>Alloy Procurement<br/><em>Planner</em></h1>
    <p class="case-deck">An 18-month material planning and purchasing decision system for approximately $3M in on-hand raw material inventory.</p>
    <div class="case-role-line"><span>System Architecture</span><span>Planning Logic</span><span>Requirements Discovery</span><span>Validation</span><span>Implementation</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-metrics case-metrics-dark">
  <div class="container case-metric-grid">
    <div><strong>20</strong><span>Alloys Planned</span></div>
    <div><strong>~18 mo.</strong><span>Planning Horizon</span></div>
    <div><strong>~5 min.</strong><span>Routine Refresh</span></div>
    <div><strong>~$3M</strong><span>On-Hand Inventory Visibility</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section">
  <div class="container case-two-col">
    <div>
      <div class="case-section-no">01</div>
      <div class="eyebrow">The Constraint</div>
      <h2>Critical material planning depended on fragmented data and one person’s experience.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="case-copy">
      <p>Alloy planning required downloading four to five separate datasets, consolidating them manually in Excel, and refreshing a pivot-based view about every two weeks. Planning typically extended no farther than six months.</p>
      <p>Purchasing rules, supplier timing, test-bar requirements, historical usage, safety-stock considerations, and special alloy behavior also lived largely in one person's working knowledge. One person had maintained the process for roughly four years before teaching it to me as they left.</p>
      <p class="case-emphasis">Alloy shortages occurred roughly two to three times per quarter. A shortage could stop affected production until replacement material arrived and completed a 2–8 week verification cycle.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-before-after">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow">Before / After</div>
    <div class="ba-grid">
      <article>
        <span class="ba-label">Before</span>
        <strong>4–5</strong><p>datasets manually downloaded and consolidated</p>
        <strong>up to ~60 min.</strong><p>to perform a routine planning update</p>
        <strong>~6 months</strong><p>of typical forward visibility</p>
        <strong>1 person</strong><p>holding most of the planning knowledge</p>
      </article>
      <div class="ba-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
      <article class="ba-after">
        <span class="ba-label">After</span>
        <strong>2 recurring refreshes</strong><p>plus a maintained scheduled-receipts table</p>
        <strong>~5 min.</strong><p>to refresh routine planning inputs</p>
        <strong>up to ~18 months</strong><p>of selectable forward planning visibility</p>
        <strong>documented</strong><p>methodology, operating instructions, and constraints</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section case-architecture">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">02</div>
    <div class="eyebrow">System Architecture</div>
    <h2>From customer demand to purchasing action.</h2>
    <p class="case-intro">The workbook converts operational exports into material requirements, reconciles supply, applies purchasing constraints, and presents decision horizons tailored to different users.</p>

    <div class="alloy-flow reveal">
      <div class="flow-inputs">
        <div class="flow-node">
          <span>Input 01</span><strong>Current Inventory</strong><small>On-hand pounds by alloy</small>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-node">
          <span>Input 02</span><strong>Customer Work Orders</strong><small>Part · Quantity · Pour Weight · Due Date</small>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-node">
          <span>Input 03</span><strong>Scheduled Receipts</strong><small>Planned · Ordered · Confirmed · ETA</small>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flow-spine"><span></span></div>

      <div class="flow-engine">
        <div class="engine-title">Planning Engine</div>
        <div class="engine-row">WO / Part <b>→</b> Alloy Mapping</div>
        <div class="engine-row">Quantity × Pour Weight <b>→</b> Material Demand</div>
        <div class="engine-row">Aggregate Demand <b>→</b> Alloy Requirements</div>
        <div class="engine-row">On Hand + Receipts − Demand <b>→</b> Running Balance</div>
        <div class="engine-row">MOQ + Lead Time + Test-Bar Timing <b>→</b> Suggested Order</div>
      </div>

      <div class="flow-spine"><span></span></div>

      <div class="flow-horizons">
        <div><strong>13 Weeks</strong><span>Immediate purchasing actions</span></div>
        <div><strong>6 Months</strong><span>Operational material readiness</span></div>
        <div><strong>1 Year</strong><span>Long-range planning</span></div>
        <div><strong>18 Months</strong><span>Supplier forecasting</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="supporting-views">
      <span>Parts by Alloy</span><span>Scheduled Receipts</span><span>Purchasing Calendar</span><span>YoY Consumption</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section case-alt">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">03</div>
    <div class="eyebrow">Design Decisions</div>
    <h2>Automate the calculation. Preserve the judgment.</h2>
    <div class="decision-grid">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Human judgment stays in the loop.</h3>
        <p>The planner suggests quantities and order timing while leaving room for customer expedites, overdue orders, business conditions, and current production priorities to shape the final decision.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Plan for plant capacity, not only supplier capacity.</h3>
        <p>The purchasing calendar staggers incoming material to avoid overloading test-bar verification or creating unnecessary mix-up risk on the production floor.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Different horizons answer different questions.</h3>
        <p>Purchasing needs the next quarter’s actions; operations needs six-month readiness; leadership and suppliers benefit from longer-range forecasting.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>04</span>
        <h3>Convert tribal knowledge into explicit constraints.</h3>
        <p>MOQ rules, supplier lead time, test-bar timing, historical consumption, special-material behavior, and planning notes are documented instead of left in one person’s memory.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section">
  <div class="container case-validation">
    <div>
      <div class="case-section-no">04</div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Validation & Iteration</div>
      <h2>A forecast is only useful if its timing reflects operational reality.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="validation-card">
      <div class="validation-old"><span>Early signal</span><strong>Risk in Q3 2027</strong><p>Quarter-level logic could imply urgency from the start of the quarter.</p></div>
      <div class="validation-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="validation-new"><span>Refined signal</span><strong>Precise Need-By Date</strong><p>The model now uses the next relevant customer due date to locate the actual material need inside the quarter.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="case-note">I validated the planner by tracing discrepancies against operational expectations and refining formulas or business logic when recommendations did not reflect the real decision.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section case-alt">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">05</div>
    <div class="eyebrow">Current State</div>
    <h2>Built, validated, documented, and entering operational use.</h2>
    <div class="current-state-grid">
      <div>
        <p>The planner entered deployment after formula validation, stakeholder review, and functional refinement with purchasing and operational leadership.</p>
        <p>Because deployment is recent, I do not yet attribute shortage reductions or inventory savings to the system. Long-term impact will be evaluated as it accumulates operating history.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="roadmap">
        <div class="eyebrow">Next Iteration</div>
        <span>Automated Data Ingestion</span>
        <span>Action Alerts</span>
        <span>Supplier Capacity Inputs</span>
        <span>Reduced Manual Copy / Paste</span>
        <span>Potential Migration Beyond Excel</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-artifact-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="artifact-head">
      <div>
        <div class="case-section-no">06</div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Working Artifact</div>
        <h2>The system, not just a screenshot.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>A portfolio version will preserve the workbook’s planning architecture and decision logic using fictionalized alloy, part, demand, and supplier data.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="artifact-placeholder artifact-alloy">
      <div class="artifact-window">
        <div class="artifact-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        <div class="artifact-skeleton">
          <div class="sk-side"></div>
          <div class="sk-main">
            <span></span><span></span><span></span>
            <div class="sk-chart"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="artifact-caption"><span>Artifact slot reserved</span><strong>Alloy Procurement Planner</strong><small>Workbook screenshots + downloadable .xlsx coming next</small></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-next">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Next System</span>
    <a href={`${base}/built-systems/onboarding-certification/`}>
      <strong>Workforce Training & Capability System</strong><span>→</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
